  <notes>Spec FR-09; design Lens 3(d) two-mode model. 033 consumes this for wizard auto-run.

Completed 2026-07-31. ONE routing decision point (ConversationPane.handleDecorateOutboundBodyWithRevise's
review-intent `if` block, ~:1768) branches explicit vs classifier — never two ifs. Explicit door:
`useAgreementReviewGate.runExplicit(fileId, fileName, subDomainKey)` — deterministic dispatch (reuses the
SAME `dispatchReview` `runGate` already uses), zero classifier gate, zero chips; the classifier still runs
NON-BLOCKING via `runClassify` for a warn-only sanity check (`resolveAgreementReviewSanityMismatch` — new
pure fn in agreementReviewRouting.ts, mirrors resolveAgreementReviewGateDecision's threshold logic) —
mismatch surfaces one informational chat message (`makeLocalAssistantMessage`, no chip/gate); classifier
error/unavailable silently produces no notice, never blocks. Classifier door: new
`agreementTypeLookupWrite.ts` module (discoverNavProps + PascalCase fallback `sprk_AgreementType`, mirrors
hub A1's mechanism per `git show 1e1a6579b` but corrects A1's still-unfixed stale `sprk_agreementtypeid`
columnName search — task 022 empirically confirmed the live column is `sprk_agreementtype`); wired into
`HistoryOverlay.tsx`'s existing "Promote to Analysis…" flow (the only client-reachable session->Analysis
bind today) via two additive optional props (`resolveClassifiedSubDomain`, `dataService`) — zero behavior
change when omitted. New `useAgreementReviewGate.getLastResolvedSubDomainKey()` tracks the classifier's
last single-type resolution (not "both" — ambiguous for a single-valued lookup; not `runExplicit` — already
persisted by its own door). 33 new tests (agreementReviewRouting +8, useAgreementReviewGate +21 across two
new describe blocks, agreementTypeLookupWrite +11 new file, ConversationPane explicit-door e2e +2 new file);
package suite 89 suites/826 tests all green (baseline 87/792); typecheck 0 surface-owned errors; `npm run
build` green. See notes/023-execution-notes.md for full detail incl. one dropped test file (Fluent v9 Menu
+ jsdom RTL-timing flakiness, unrelated to production correctness — decision documented).</notes>
